% Daml intro, Daml Script: tokens a party may only issue to itself
%
% The Logical English (for LPS) twin of a Daml project, written by the Daml translator
% from its source: each template a fluent keyed by the contract id, each create and choice an action,
% who may do what integrity constraints. The source is kept in sources/ (File > Show the Original in the
% Logical English editor, View > The original this was converted from in the LPS2 IDE).
% The ids of the contracts a command creates are places of its action: the ledger assigns them, a scenario names them.
% Who may do what, as one permission per command: the legal view
% (Misc > Legal View of This LPS Program in the Logical English editor, View > Legal view in the LPS2 IDE).

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 8.

the actions are:
    *a party* creates the token *a token* with owner *an owner*; known as create_token.
    *a party* archives the token *a token*; known as archive_token.

the fluents are:
    *a token* is a token with owner *an owner*; known as token.

the knowledge base token includes:

the text of "the source daml/Token_Test.daml" is at "sources/daml/Token_Test.daml".

% Token: a party creates one; its signatories must be the one who submits (Daml's authorization)
when a party creates the token a token with owner an owner
then the token is a token with owner the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the token a token with owner an owner
    and the party is different from the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party creates the token a token with owner an owner
    and the token is a token with owner a second owner.

% Token: archiving one (Daml's Archive choice) is for its signatories, and it must be active
when a party archives the token a token
    and the token is a token with owner an owner
then it is not the case that the token is a token with owner the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the token a token
    and the token is a token with owner an owner
    and the party is different from the owner.

it must not be true that
    a party archives the token a token
    and it is not the case that the token is a token with owner an owner.

% Daml (the script run on a Canton sandbox) ends with these active contracts (their payloads;
% the ids are the ledger's):
%   - token(alice)
% The twin's final state under LPS2 (`lps state`) is compared with it by test_daml.pl.
scenario token_test is:
    % the Daml Script token_test
    alice creates the token c1 with owner alice from 1 to 2.
    bob creates the token bob_token with owner bob from 2 to 3.
    % Daml refuses the next command (submitMustFail): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    alice creates the token c2 with owner bob from 3 to 4.
    % Daml refuses the next command (submitMustFail): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    bob creates the token c3 with owner alice from 4 to 5.
    % Daml refuses the next command (submitMustFail): the twin's integrity constraints refuse it
    alice archives the token bob_token from 5 to 6.
    bob archives the token bob_token from 6 to 7.

